the FBI is investigating a potential  hate crime in American University in  Washington students found several  bananas Monday hanging from small ropes  Todd Lake nooses racist racist messages  were written on the bananas campus  police released two surveillance videos  Tuesday of a possible suspect a thousand  dollar reward is being offered for  information leading to the person chip  Reid is outside the American University  campus in Washington where students are  on edge chip good morning  well good morning this is not the first  racist incident here at American  University in September white two  students were accused of throwing a  banana at one black student and leaving  a rotten banana in the dorm room of  another this latest incident happened on  the same day that a black woman became  student body president a first for this  university surveillance video shows a  person dressed in black early Monday  morning approaching two of the locations  where the racist messages were placed  the bananas had the words harambe bait  and AKA free written on them police  believe they referenced Alpha Kappa  Alpha the predominantly black sorority  where the new student body president  Taylor dumps in' is a member hate and  racism and bigotry have no place on this  campus and that's not we want here on  this university not as a student not a  student government president and on  behalf of the AU community that is not  what we need here and this is not what  we need anywhere in this country Terry  Flenory is vice president of  communications at the University we made  some direct outreach to the students who  are members of Alpha Kappa Alpha and  immediately worked to identify what we  could do to support them and make them  feel safe but some don't think it's  enough on Tuesday students marched  across campus in protest and walked out  of a town hall meeting yeah it's all  really frustrating Danyelle Jermaine is  the social media chair for the black  students Alliance he saw 